# The pc platform's polar Aku Aku test (#1093, docs/platforms.md), played
# with --level 3 --room 1 (Frostbite Cavern's polar stage):
# platform/pc/preview.keys's Start and A through the logos and menus to the
# level select (frames 1-514), which picks the level and room, then a ride
# on the polar bear that breaks a crate for Aku Aku's first mask (~826)
# and is hit with it (~917): Aku Aku, losing its last mask, loads the
# palette 0x20 bytes before gPolarAkuAkuPalette1, the four 12-byte boxes
# before it in the ROM, for the 39 frames of its animation. The host laid
# those boxes out 16 bytes apart, and those frames' colours were other
# than mGBA's until polar_palettes_boxes.cpp aligned them (and the
# palette) to 4 bytes. tools/boottest.py `screens` (the same
# --level and --room) played it on mGBA for
# tests/polar_mask_mgba_screens.json, every 3rd frame: all the same
# (frame 512, the first after the level's load, differs, see
# docs/platforms.md, and isn't a 3rd).
# Written by a search over the host's runs (random steering until the
# mask was lost without a death).
# A line `FRAME KEYS` holds KEYS from FRAME on (platform/pc/src/input.c).
